<ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/amiriya-madrasa"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/amiriya-madrasa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Amiriya Madrasa</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Amiriya Madrasa is a religious school and mosque in Rada'a, Yemen, built by the Tahirid sultan Amir ibn Abd al-Wahhab and completed in 1504.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/amiternum"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/amiternum.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Amiternum</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Amiternum was an ancient Sabine town in the upper Aterno valley of central Italy, near modern L'Aquila.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/al-amjad-bahramshah"><span class="enc-name">Al-Amjad Bahramshah</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Al-Amjad Bahramshah was the Ayyubid emir of Baalbek from 1182 to 1230, son of Saladin's nephew Farrukh Shah.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/amlaib-conung"><span class="enc-name">Amlaíb Conung</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Amlaíb Conung was a Viking leader who, according to the Irish annals, arrived in Ireland in 853 and ruled the Norse of Dublin with Ímar.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/amlapura"><span class="enc-name">Amlapura</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Amlapura is a town in eastern Bali, Indonesia, and the capital of Karangasem Regency.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/amm"><span class="enc-name">Amm</span><span class="enc-type">Religion / idea</span><span class="enc-snip">Amm was the national god of the ancient South Arabian kingdom of Qataban in Yemen, often thought to be a moon